   520	## 8. Derivation firewalls and affine-plane controls
   521	
   522	Three distinctions are essential.
   523	
   524	1. A derivation with a slice need not be locally nilpotent, even if locally
   525	   finite.  On `C[x,y]`,
   526	
   527	   ```text
   528	   D=partial_x+y partial_y,       D(x)=1
   529	   ```
   530	
   531	   is the smallest control.  Its divergence for `dx wedge dy` is one, so it
   532	   does not contradict Section 5.
   533	
   534	2. Volume preservation plus a slice is not the same as Hamiltonianity on a
   535	   surface with nonzero first de Rham cohomology.  On
   536	   `C[s,t,t^(-1)]`, `D=partial_s+t partial_t` preserves
   537	   `ds wedge dt/t` and has slice `s`, but
   538	
   539	   ```text
   540	   i_D(ds wedge dt/t)=dt/t-ds
   541	   ```
   542	
   543	   is not algebraically exact.  The exact pseudo-plane is Q-acyclic and our
   544	   derivations are explicitly Hamiltonian, so this control only prevents an
   545	   overgeneralization.
   546	
   547	3. On `A2`, a universal assertion
   548	
   549	   ```text
   550	   Hamiltonian derivation with a polynomial slice => locally nilpotent
   551	   ```
   552	
   553	   is equivalent to JC2.  Indeed `X_f(g)=1` is exactly a Keller pair
   554	   `{f,g}=1`.  If `X_f` is locally nilpotent, Rentschler plus the slice theorem
   555	   makes `(f,g)` a polynomial coordinate pair; the converse is immediate.
   556	   Hence no affine-plane derivation lemma of this strength is available as an
   557	   independent input.
   558	
   559	## 9. Theorem/gap map and cheapest successors
   560	
   561	The exact status is:
   562	
   563	| Proposed route | Exact result | Status for the horn |
   564	|---|---|---|
   565	| LND plus slice | Impossible by `Pic(R)=Z/2` | branch closed |
   566	| Locally finite Hamiltonian plus slice | Locally finite implies LND by Sections 4--6 | branch closed |
   567	| ML / Derksen | Both equal `C[A]` | only detects algebraic additive flows |
   568	| Picard torsion | `eta^*:Pic(R)->Pic(R)` can be zero | no etale functorial obstruction |
   569	| Unique additive `A1`-ruling | A Keller coordinate has non-`A1` generic fibre; (7.1) also moves `A` to `U^2` | rules out only the `A1`-fibre branch |
   570	| Smooth `C*` fibration | `U` is smooth with generic fibre `C*`, but has no slice; a Keller coordinate cannot have generic fibre `C*` | branch closed |
   571	| Etale selfmaps | Exact degree-two nonproper family exists | firewall, not map to `A2` |
   572	| Mixed/mixed Keller pair | Both Hamiltonian flows must be non-locally-finite | open |
   573	
   574	The highest-value exact successors are now:
   575	
   576	1. **Boundary-to-algebraic-flow gate.**  Prove that the charged quartic
   577	   `(3,1)+(2,2)` packet makes at least one of the two commuting Hamiltonian
   578	   flows locally finite.  The theorem above would then close the horn
   579	   immediately.  Without the boundary packet this is false as a plausible
   580	   general principle and risks restating JC2.
   581	2. **Hyperbolic fibre classification.**  Each coordinate of a Keller pair
   582	   defines a smooth surjection with generic fibre neither `A1` nor `C*`.
   583	   Enumerate the degree-four completion data in (6.9), then couple its finite
   584	   deleted points and points over infinity to the charged boundary census.
   585	3. **Wild-flow filtration.**  Use (0.3) and the hyperbolic weights
   586	   `(2,1,-2)` to study a non-locally-finite `X_H` with a slice.  A successful
   587	   theorem must consume the exact index-four field condition or boundary
   588	   valuations.  Merely taking a highest homogeneous term cannot discard
   589	   cancellations at the retained fibre.
   590	4. **Etale-to-plane classification.**  Separate maps `R->R`, for which (7.1)
   591	   supplies abundant countercontrols, from maps `C[s,t]->R` whose two images
   592	   form an exact symplectic coframe.  The latter is the genuinely missing
   593	   classification.
   594	
   595	Do not promote an exclusion of the mixed/mixed one-cusp horn, local
   596	nilpotence of an arbitrary Hamiltonian slice, functoriality of ML/Derksen or
   597	Pic under etale maps, or preservation of the ruling by nonproper etale
   598	endomorphisms.  No heavy computation is justified by this result.
