   248	## 4. Applying the distinction to the saturated horn
   249	
   250	### 4.1 Collision outside `B`
   251	
   252	At a point outside `B`, `pi` is finite etale and the quartic cover splits
   253	strict-henselian locally into four sections.  The two points with equal
   254	ruling value are interior points of `U`; no source boundary component is
   255	created.  Their equality divisor in the target is not in the outer sum of
   256	(2.1).
   257	
   258	Each deleted cyclic line contains corresponding copies of the two
   259	normalization points of `C_0`.  The finite completion is etale along those
   260	lines.  At each point separately, the local multiplicity in Orevkov's sense
   261	is one.  Thus the line's bracket remains
   262	
   263	```text
   264	mu_l+sum_x(mu_x-mu_l)=1+0.                              (4.1)
   265	```
   266	
   267	The node is a global failure of injectivity of the line parametrization,
   268	not a local failure of etaleness.
   269	
   270	### 4.2 Collision at an ordinary point of `B`
   271	
   272	The completed quartic algebra has one rank-two ramified factor and two
   273	unramified companion factors.  The collision occurs on the two companion
   274	points in `U`.  The point on the ramification boundary `R` is distinct.
   275	Equality of the two companion values gives no condition on the value or
   276	pole order of `t` at that third point.  Hence the generic boundary term two
   277	over `B` does not jump to three.
   278	
   279	The unique `(3,1)` cusp jump is already charged in (1.2), and the omitted
   280	`(2,2)` point is not on `C_0`.  Nothing in (3.4) moves the ordinary collision
   281	to either special value.
   282	
   283	### 4.3 Meeting infinity is not enough
   284	
   285	The projective closure of the affine index curve must meet the line at
   286	infinity, but (2.1) does not count target intersection with infinity.  It
   287	counts local multiplicity of the regularized source map.  A transversal
   288	meeting of the index curve with an existing boundary image can occur while
   289	the source map remains a local biholomorphism.  A positive correction needs
   290	the additional implication
   291	
   292	```text
   293	closure(J_t) meets boundary  =>  mu_x>mu_l,             (4.2)
   294	```
   295	
   296	and (4.2) is false for general etale orders and formal boundary maps.
