    86	   The ruling and `pi` are unrelated morphisms.  A principal cusp-node curve
    87	   already coexists with a componentwise-irreducible `A1`-ruling on `A2`;
    88	   Section 6 gives the exact control.  A contradiction requires a new theorem
    89	   coupling `rho` to `pi`, not only the existence of the curve `T`.
    90	
    91	The sharp remaining target is therefore a **pseudo-plane-to-plane gate**:
    92	exclude an etale quasi-finite rank-four map satisfying (0.2)--(0.4), or prove
    93	that the actual first leg forces the companion closure to extend
    94	principally.  Neither conclusion follows from the present local packets.
